 "caption": "A cell is fed through its surface but burns fuel throughout its volume. For a sphere A/V = 3/r, so doubling the radius gives each bit of the inside half as much membrane. That's why cells stay tiny and why lungs and guts fold into huge surfaces.\n\nSave this for your biology course.\n\n#biology #cellbiology #math #geometry #science #stem #physiology #learnscience",
